# B108 - hard-coded temp path. ONE site left, and it is the one with the real
# story: the deploy lock's predictable path in a world-writable directory IS
# the cross-user mutual-exclusion mechanism, so moving it (per-uid, or
# $TMPDIR-derived) would clear this finding by deleting the property the lock
# exists for. #1113 hardened the OPEN instead - O_NOFOLLOW against a symlink
# whose target `open(path,"w")` truncated, O_NONBLOCK + S_ISREG against a FIFO
# that hung the deploy - and accepted the finding with that reasoning recorded
# in docs/security/bandit-finding-dispositions.md.
#
# `lib/cicd/runner.py B108` was here and is CLOSED (#1113): the uv cache had no
# such contract to preserve, so it became a uid-scoped path created 0700 and
# validated for symlink, type, owner and group/other-writability before use.
finding lib/cicd/deploy/guardrails.py B108 1 #1113

# B310 - CLOSED, both sites (#1113). They carried `# noqa: S310` and a comment
# asserting a fixed https host; the comment is now code. A scheme check alone
# would NOT have cleared these - B310 is a call blacklist with no dataflow - so
# what closed them is that neither site calls `urllib.request.urlopen` any
# more: both use an OpenerDirector registering only https handlers, which
# cannot open `file:` or `ftp:` at all, plus an initial-URL check and a
# redirect-target check (urllib's default handler permits an https -> http
# downgrade). See the register's B310 section before reverting any of it.

